0", "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pulls/234", "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR", "_links": {"html": {"href": "https://github.com/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pull/234#pullrequestreview-4901786690"}, "pull_request": {"href": "https://api.github.com/repos/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pulls/234"}}, "submitted_at": "2026-08-10T23:37:57Z", "commit_id": "e30578906259c270314b52e72f6a7c12871a1fae"}, {"id": 4904117451, "node_id": "PRR_kwDON3RSpc8AAAABJE7kyw", "user": {"login": "keewis", "id": 14808389, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODA4Mzg5", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14808389?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis", "html_url": "https://github.com/keewis", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pull/234#pullrequestreview-4904117451", "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pulls/234", "author_association": "MEMBER", "_links": {"html": {"href": "https://github.com/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pull/234#pullrequestreview-4904117451"}, "pull_request": {"href": "https://api.github.com/repos/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pulls/234"}}, "submitted_at": "2026-08-11T08:02:27Z", "commit_id": "ca8ff1ec9b203eba9bbe8154a7a682e2d6865e30"}, {"id": 4904167879, "node_id": "PRR_kwDON3RSpc8AAAABJE-pxw", "user": {"login": "keewis", "id": 14808389, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODA4Mzg5", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14808389?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis", "html_url": "https://github.com/keewis", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/keewis/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "once again this looks mostly good, but I've got a few small comments.\r\n\r\nIn particular, I'd argue we shouldn't have tests that check the absence of old API. This may be fine to make sure it is actually gone, but in the long run I think this just gets confusing.\r\n\r\nAlso, I think since we are defining a new API I think now is a good point in time to decide whether to name the size parameter `depth` (used by `cdshealpix`) or `level` (used by DGGS in general, short for \"refinement level\"). In the python bindings I kinda did both: `depth` for the low-level API and `level` for the grid object. I don't know that that was a good choice (as-in, I've yet to decide), but I think for the JS bindings we don't have to follow the python bindings. Either way, most of this is used in the geo context, so I'd lean towards following the DGGS terminology.\r\n\r\nAs for your questions:\r\n1. `toScheme`: this is tricky. In #236 I've added a additional `level` parameter to the function that allows specifying the refinement levels, but only if we convert to a scheme that encodes the level in the cell ids (right now only `zuniq`, but I've had the request to also add `nuniq`, and maybe your own indexing scheme... if I remember correctly, that was called `mortie`?)\r\n2. `Ellipsoid.from`: the validation is great. I added a point on obliqueness in the comments, and now that I think about it we _could_ support `inverse_flattening: 0` to mean `flattening: 0`, but that's for another day.\r\n3. Naming: yeah, I think the names should be similar so it is easy to know that they do the same thing (see also one of the comments below)\r\n4. `vertex`'s `u`, `v` parameters: I think we should be strict and validate to `[0, 1]`. These are defined to start at the southern axis and propagate forwards, so there would need to be some validation code that checks the coordinate moves out of the projection plane's domain (i.e. the triangular gaps around the northern polar cap)\r\n5. `@types/node`: how complicated would it make the loading of the declarations without it? If it is not too complicated I'd say let's try to avoid the dependency, otherwise it's fine to keep it. Somewhat unrelated, but while doing a quick search on `vitest` I found https://vitest.dev/guide/testing-types.html which claims that `vitest --typechecking` replaces `tsc --noEmit`", "state": "COMMENTED", "html_url": "https://github.com/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pull/234#pullrequestreview-4904167879", "pull_request_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pulls/234", "author_association": "MEMBER", "_links": {"html": {"href": "https://github.com/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pull/234#pullrequestreview-4904167879"}, "pull_request": {"href": "https://api.github.com/repos/GRID4EARTH/healpix-geo/pulls/234"}}, "submitted_at": "2026-08-11T10:27:44Z", "commit_id": "e30578906259c270314b52e72f6a7c12871a1fae"}, {"id": 4912147343, "node_id": "PRR_kwDON3RSpc8AAAABJMlrjw", "user": {"login": "espg", "id": 3